   "description": "LOOK-BRIEF Phase 1 mood: dusk. Amber sun near the horizon (12 deg) further round to the back-left, so vertical faces catch amber light and the shadows run long; a lavender hemisphere sky makes the shadows read lavender; deeper blue-violet zenith, amber-peach horizon on the sun side, lavender-pink away from it. Day-cycle keyframe 19.5 h. PHASE 2: materials (Worldseed-leaning: moderate saturation, hue contrast). Grass = three greens (warm yellow-green / mid / cool deep) blended by a 15 u world-space noise, lusher + cooler near water, drier on high ground, darker at cliff feet and under woods (vertex colours by the core, per vertex). Warm red-brown taupe stone, lighter top edges, darker feet; the underside reads as warm brown rock and fades gently into the haze below. Canopies: bottom-to-top gradient, per-tree tints, moderated saturation, leaf translucency (conifers deep green, never black). Clouds: fewer, none in front of the farm (+ simple cream / lavender shading; the next stage replaces them). Gameplay cameras: zenith blue at the top of the screen. Grass + stone colours are albedo (identical in every mood). Cloud tops rose-cream, undersides violet. LOOK CORE (WORLDSEED-BRIEF): Worldseed-family lawn (warmer, greener: lit meadow hue 85-105 deg, sat 0.40-0.50), canopies toward the Worldseed foliage ramp, near-black albedos lifted to a coloured dark; painted sky + cloud sea (periwinkle shade, cream caps) instead of the puff clouds and the deck; cel-banded Lambert (terminator 0.26, violet shade fill, warm rim); one composite pass (plum depth ink, Neutral once, selective bloom, split-tone grade, vignette); seam lips match the grass.",
